# Ecosystem short-form alias: /address/{G} (EVM/Bitcoin habit) → /accounts/{G}
# (Stellar's native term + Horizon convention). Clean path redirect (no query
# string), so a _redirects 301 is correct. SEO plan D-redirect set.
/address/*  /accounts/:splat  301

# Singular short aliases for the two graph boards' per-address pages.
# /sponsor/{G} and /creator/{G} are what a reader types or is handed; the
# canonical page lives under the board it belongs to, the same shape as
# /address/{G} → /accounts/{G} above. The splat carries the G-strkey
# through untouched — these are case-SENSITIVE base32, and a rule that
# lowercased one would send every link to a nonexistent account.
#
# Bare form too: /sponsor and /creator alone name no address, so they go
# to the board rather than to a detail page with nothing in it. Listed
# with and without the trailing slash because next.js's trailingSlash 308
# fires on the explorer's OWN routes, not on aliases it does not serve.
/sponsor           /insights/sponsors/             301
/sponsor/          /insights/sponsors/             301
/sponsor/*         /insights/sponsors/:splat       301
/creator           /insights/creators/             301
/creator/          /insights/creators/             301
/creator/*         /insights/creators/:splat       301

# Dashboard relocated /account/* → /dashboard/* (SEO plan, dashboard is noindex;
# entities use plural /accounts/{g}). Keep old bookmarks working.
/account            /dashboard/         301
/account/           /dashboard/         301
/account/*          /dashboard/:splat   301

# /protocols/sdex → /sdex (2026-08-24 sdex unification, PR #143's server
# half). The Next page does permanentRedirect, but under static export
# that ships an __next_error__ shell that only redirects after JS
# hydration — crawlers and no-JS agents saw a 200 error shell. This
# rule makes it a real HTTP 301. Trailing-slash form only (next.js
# trailingSlash 308s the bare form first, same as /currencies rules).
/protocols/sdex/  /sdex/  301

